From 498414811a8119c5b447b3a96ec92ab5736cba3f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Williams <patrick@stwcx.xyz>
Date: Wed, 5 Mar 2025 16:12:45 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] State: add generic CPER notification events

Define generic Common Platform Error Record (CPER) notification
events for use with phosphor-logging.

These events provide lightweight notification and classification
for CPER-derived log entries. They are not intended to transport
decoded CPER contents or other diagnostic data.

A Source object may be provided to associate the resulting log
entry with the platform component related to the reported CPER event.

CPER-specific diagnostic information is expected to be exposed
through log-entry extension interfaces associated with the created
log entry. Such extensions may provide summarized diagnostic
information, decoded CPER content, references to supplemental
diagnostic artifacts, inventory associations, serviceability
information, and vendor-specific metadata.

The distinction between Error and Information is intended to align
with phosphor-logging prioritization, lifecycle management, and
retention behavior. Detailed CPER severity information remains
part of the associated CPER diagnostic content and is not encoded
in the event definition itself.

Future CPER-specific event definitions may provide finer-grained
classification should common requirements emerge.

